module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.IdealSmulAffineObjectwise

/-!
# Generators of the inverse-image ideal of a representable morphism

Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a representable morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` contained in a
big fppf site `B` and let `I ⊆ 𝒪_X` be a sheaf of ideals on the small étale site of `X`.  The
inverse-image ideal `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackIdealSubsheaf` is built as the infimum of the
sheaves of ideals of `𝒪_Y` containing the pulled-back sections `f♯(a)`, which makes *membership*
in it easy to use and the ideal itself opaque.  This file replaces that description by generators:
the objectwise ideal generated by the restrictions of the pulled-back sections has the
inverse-image ideal as its closure, so a section of `f⁻¹I · 𝒪_Y` is locally a combination of
restricted pulled-back sections, and likewise a section of `f⁻¹I · F` is locally a combination of
products of those with sections of `F`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackIdealGenerators` is the set of restrictions, to an étale chart
  `W` of `Y` admitting a morphism to a base-changed chart `Q ×_X Y`, of the pullbacks `f♯(a)` of
  the sections of `I` over `Q`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackIdealPresheaf` is the objectwise ideal they span.
* `Stacks.Sites.presheafSmul` is the objectwise product of an *objectwise* sheaf of ideals with an
  objectwise submodule of a sheaf of modules, generalizing `Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackIdealSubsheaf_eq_sheafifySubmodule`: **the inverse-image ideal
  is the closure of the objectwise ideal generated by the restricted pulled-back sections.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_pullbackIdealSubsheaf_iff`: a section of `𝒪_Y` lies in the
  inverse-image ideal exactly when it is, locally, a combination of restricted pulled-back
  sections.
* `Stacks.Sites.idealSmul_sheafifySubmodule_eq`: the product of the closure of an objectwise sheaf
  of ideals with a submodule is the closure of the objectwise product, so taking the closure of
  the ideal first costs nothing.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf_iff`: **a section of `f⁻¹I · F` is
  locally a combination of products of a restricted pulled-back section of `I` with a section of
  `F`**, which is the description that the descent of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_presheafIdealSmul_of_mem_idealSmul_of_isAffine` consumes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_idealSmul_of_forall_isAffine`: membership in `I · f_*F` over an
  étale chart of `X` follows from objectwise membership over the affine charts above it, which is
  the reduction of Stacks 0GF8 to an affine chart of `X`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_presheafIdealSmul_iff_mem_pushforwardIdealMultipleSections` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_presheafIdealSmul_iff_mem_pullbackIdealMultipleSections`: the
  objectwise product `I · f_*F` over a chart `Q` of `X` is the ideal multiple
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pushforwardIdealMultipleSections` of sections, hence also the multiple
  of `F(Q ×_X Y)` by the ideal generated by the pulled-back sections.  This is what connects the
  sheaf-level product to the chart-sections identity
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ideal_smul_pushforward_sections_eq_of_representable`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_span_image_restrict_of_mem_map_smul`: over the smaller of two
  affine charts of `Y`, the multiple of the sections of `F` by a restricted ideal is spanned by
  the restrictions of the multiple over the larger one.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_presheafIdealSmul_of_mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_idealSmul_pushforward_of_mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf`: the
  opposite inclusion of Stacks 0GF8, granted the two hypotheses recorded in the implementation
  notes below.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul` takes a sheaf of ideals, that is, one whose membership is already
local, and `Stacks.Sites.idealSmul` is its closure.  Both products appearing here have an
objectwise ideal as their left factor, so `Stacks.Sites.presheafSmul` takes an objectwise one; it
agrees with `Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul` on a sheaf of ideals by
`Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul_eq_presheafSmul`, which is `rfl`.

The generators are indexed by a morphism `W ⟶ Q ×_X Y` of étale charts of `Y` rather than by the
chart `W` alone, because small-chart base change does not reach every chart of `Y`: a chart of `Y`
admits such a morphism only locally, which is why the objectwise ideal has to be closed up.

*What the opposite inclusion of Stacks 0GF8 still needs.*
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_idealSmul_pushforward_of_mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf` proves
it from two hypotheses, and those two are the whole of what is left of the tag.

The first is that the base change `Q ×_X Y` of an affine chart `Q` of `X` is an affine chart of
`Y`.  This holds when `f` is affine, which is the hypothesis of the source, and is not available
in the tree: `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.representablePullbackMap_property` with
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineHom` gives affineness of the base change of a *morphism* of charts, not
of the base-changed chart itself, whose structure morphism `Q ×_X Y ⟶ Q` is not a morphism of the
site.  What it needs is the representability square
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallBaseChange_isPullback`, then
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsAffineHom.of_isPullback` to see the projection as an affine morphism
of spaces, and then the affine object representing its base change along the identity of `Q`.

The second is that over an affine chart `V` of `Y` carrying a morphism to a base-changed affine
chart `Q ×_X Y`, the objectwise inverse-image ideal is already generated by the sections pulled
back from that single chart `Q`.  A generator of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackIdealPresheaf`
over `V` comes from some other chart `Q'` of `X` through a morphism `V ⟶ Q' ×_X Y`, and comparing
it with the generators from `Q` means comparing both over the product `Q ×_X Q'`, which is a chart
of `X` because `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.instHasBinaryProducts`; there `I` is cartesian
on affine charts, so `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartIdeal_map_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts` relates
the sections of `I` over an affine chart of `Q ×_X Q'` to those over `Q`, and the structure map
`f♯` carries that relation to `Y` by naturality.  The step that is missing is the morphism from
`V` into `(Q ×_X Q') ×_X Y`: `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.preservesPullbacks_smallBaseChange` is
preservation of fibre products over an object of the site, and the small étale site of an
algebraic space has no terminal object, so it does not say that small-chart base change carries
the product `Q ×_X Q'` to the product of `Q ×_X Y` and `Q' ×_X Y`, which is what the universal
property of the latter would consume.  The inequality is local on `V`, by the same faithfully flat
descent that `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_span_image_restrict_of_mem_map_smul` uses, so a covering
family of `V` by charts admitting such a morphism would suffice.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GF8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GF8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03G8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03G8)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe w v₁ u₁ m u

namespace Stacks.Sites


variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] {O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{u}}
  {M : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)}

/-- **The objectwise product `A · N` of an objectwise sheaf of ideals with an objectwise submodule
of a sheaf of modules**: over every object of the site, the submodule spanned by the products of a
section of `A` with a section of `N`.

This is `Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul` with the locality of membership in the left factor
dropped; the two agree on a sheaf of ideals by
`Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul_eq_presheafSmul`. -/
noncomputable def presheafSmul
    (A : (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)).val.Submodule)
    (N : M.val.Submodule) : M.val.Submodule where
  obj X := Submodule.span ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.obj X)
    {z : M.val.obj X | ∃ a : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.obj X,
      a ∈ A.obj X ∧ ∃ m ∈ N.obj X, z = a • m}
  map {X Y} g := by
    refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_
    rintro z ⟨a, ha, m, hm, rfl⟩
    refine Submodule.mem_comap.2 ?_
    change M.val.map g (a • m) ∈ _
    rw [M.val.map_smul]
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨_, A.map_mem g ha, _, N.map_mem g hm, rfl⟩

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat)] in
/-- A product of a section of `A` with a section of `N` is a section of the objectwise product. -/
theorem smul_mem_presheafSmul
    {A : (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)).val.Submodule}
    {N : M.val.Submodule} {X : Cᵒᵖ} {a : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.obj X}
    (ha : a ∈ A.obj X) {m : M.val.obj X} (hm : m ∈ N.obj X) :
    a • m ∈ (presheafSmul A N).obj X :=
  Submodule.subset_span ⟨a, ha, m, hm, rfl⟩

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat)] in
/-- The objectwise product is the smallest objectwise submodule containing every product of a
section of `A` with a section of `N`. -/
theorem presheafSmul_le
    {A : (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)).val.Submodule}
    {N P : M.val.Submodule}
    (h : ∀ (X : Cᵒᵖ) (a : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.obj X), a ∈ A.obj X →
      ∀ m ∈ N.obj X, a • m ∈ P.obj X) : presheafSmul A N ≤ P :=
  fun X => Submodule.span_le.2 (by rintro z ⟨a, ha, m, hm, rfl⟩; exact h X a ha m hm)

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat)] in
/-- On a sheaf of ideals the objectwise product of `Stacks.Sites.presheafSmul` is the one of
`Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul`. -/
theorem presheafIdealSmul_eq_presheafSmul (I : IdealSubsheaf O) (N : M.val.Submodule) :
    presheafIdealSmul I N = presheafSmul I.toSubmodule N :=
  rfl

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat)] in
/-- **Closing up the ideal first costs nothing**: the product of the closure of an objectwise
sheaf of ideals with a submodule of a sheaf of modules is the closure of the objectwise product.

A product `a · m` with `a` lying locally in `A` lies locally in the objectwise product, which is
the inclusion that is not formal. -/
theorem idealSmul_sheafifySubmodule_eq
    (A : (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)).val.Submodule)
    (N : M.Submodule) :
    idealSmul (Stacks.SheafOfModules.sheafifySubmodule A) N =
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.sheafifySubmodule (presheafSmul A N.toSubmodule) := by
  refine le_antisymm (Stacks.SheafOfModules.sheafifySubmodule_le
    (presheafIdealSmul_le _ fun Z a ha m hm => ?_)) (Stacks.SheafOfModules.sheafifySubmodule_le
      (presheafSmul_le fun Z a ha m hm => ?_))
  · obtain ⟨T, hT, hmem⟩ := Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_sieve_of_mem_sheafifySubmodule ha
    refine Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_sheafifySubmodule_of_mem hT fun V g hg => ?_
    rw [M.val.map_smul]
    exact smul_mem_presheafSmul (hmem g hg) (N.toSubmodule.map_mem g.op hm)
  · exact smul_mem_idealSmul _ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.le_sheafifySubmodule A Z ha) hm

end Stacks.Sites

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

noncomputable section

attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isContinuous_smallBaseChange

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
variable {X Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (f : Y ⟶ X)
  (hf : yoneda.relativelyRepresentable f.hom)
  (I : (SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2)).Submodule)

/-! ### Generators of the inverse-image ideal -/

/-- **The sections generating the inverse-image ideal over an étale chart `W` of `Y`**: the
restrictions along a morphism `W ⟶ Q ×_X Y` of the pullback `f♯(a)` of a section `a` of `I` over
an étale chart `Q` of `X`. -/
def pullbackIdealGenerators (W : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1) :
    Set ((SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)).val.obj (op W)) :=
  {z | ∃ (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (w : W ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q)
    (a : chartSectionsRing B S hS X Q), a ∈ chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I Q ∧
      z = (SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)).val.map w.op
        (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q a)}

/-- **The objectwise inverse-image ideal**: over every étale chart of `Y`, the ideal generated by
the restricted pullbacks of the sections of `I`.

Its closure is the inverse-image ideal, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackIdealSubsheaf_eq_sheafifySubmodule`. -/
def pullbackIdealPresheaf :
    (SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)).val.Submodule where
  obj W := Submodule.span (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y W.unop)
    (pullbackIdealGenerators B S hS f hf I W.unop)
  map {W V} g := by
    refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_
    rintro z ⟨Q, w, a, ha, rfl⟩
    refine Submodule.mem_comap.2 (Submodule.subset_span ⟨Q, g.unop ≫ w, a, ha, ?_⟩)
    exact ((SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)).val.map_comp_apply
      w.op g _).symm

/-- The restricted pullback of a section of `I` is a section of the objectwise inverse-image
ideal. -/
theorem map_chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_pullbackIdealPresheaf {W : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1}
    (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (w : W ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q)
    {a : chartSectionsRing B S hS X Q} (ha : a ∈ chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I Q) :
    (SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)).val.map w.op
        (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q a) ∈
      (pullbackIdealPresheaf B S hS f hf I).obj (op W) :=
  Submodule.subset_span ⟨Q, w, a, ha, rfl⟩

/-- Every sheaf of ideals of `𝒪_Y` bounding the inverse-image ideal contains the objectwise
inverse-image ideal: it contains the pullbacks of the sections of `I` by assumption, hence their
restrictions, hence the ideal they generate. -/
theorem pullbackIdealPresheaf_le_of_isPullbackIdealUpperBound
    {P : (SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)).Submodule}
    (hP : IsPullbackIdealUpperBound B S hS f hf I P) :
    pullbackIdealPresheaf B S hS f hf I ≤ P.toSubmodule := by
  intro W
  refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_
  rintro z ⟨Q, w, a, ha, rfl⟩
  exact P.toSubmodule.map_mem w.op (hP Q a ha)

/-- The closure of the objectwise inverse-image ideal bounds the inverse-image ideal: over every
chart above the base-changed chart `Q ×_X Y` the restriction of a pulled-back section of `I` is a
generator, so the pulled-back section lies in the objectwise ideal along the whole sieve of
arrows into `Q ×_X Y`. -/
theorem isPullbackIdealUpperBound_sheafifySubmodule :
    IsPullbackIdealUpperBound B S hS f hf I
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.sheafifySubmodule (pullbackIdealPresheaf B S hS f hf I)) :=
  fun Q _ ha => Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_sheafifySubmodule_of_mem
    ((SmallEtale.topology B S hS Y.1).top_mem _)
    fun _ w _ => map_chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_pullbackIdealPresheaf B S hS f hf I Q w ha

/-- **The inverse-image ideal is the closure of the objectwise ideal generated by the restricted
pullbacks of the sections of `I`.**

The closure is a sheaf of ideals bounding the inverse-image ideal, so the infimum defining the
latter is at most the closure; and the objectwise ideal is contained in every bound, in
particular in the infimum, so the closure is at most the infimum. -/
theorem pullbackIdealSubsheaf_eq_sheafifySubmodule :
    pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I =
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.sheafifySubmodule (pullbackIdealPresheaf B S hS f hf I) :=
  le_antisymm
    (pullbackIdealSubsheaf_le B S hS f hf I
      (isPullbackIdealUpperBound_sheafifySubmodule B S hS f hf I))
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.sheafifySubmodule_le
      (pullbackIdealPresheaf_le_of_isPullbackIdealUpperBound B S hS f hf I
        (isPullbackIdealUpperBound_pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I)))

/-- **A section of `𝒪_Y` lies in the inverse-image ideal exactly when it is locally a combination
of restricted pullbacks of the sections of `I`.** -/
theorem mem_pullbackIdealSubsheaf_iff {W : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1}
    {s : chartSectionsRing B S hS Y W} :
    s ∈ (pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I).obj (op W) ↔
      ∃ T : Sieve W, T ∈ SmallEtale.topology B S hS Y.1 W ∧
        ∀ ⦃V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1⦄ (g : V ⟶ W), T g →
          (SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)).val.map g.op s ∈
            (pullbackIdealPresheaf B S hS f hf I).obj (op V) := by
  rw [pullbackIdealSubsheaf_eq_sheafifySubmodule]
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_sheafifySubmodule_iff

/-! ### Generators of the multiple of a module by the inverse-image ideal -/

variable (F : SheafOfModules.{m} (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2))

/-- **The multiple `f⁻¹I · F` is the closure of the objectwise product of the objectwise
inverse-image ideal with `F`.**  Closing the ideal up before multiplying costs nothing, by
`Stacks.Sites.idealSmul_sheafifySubmodule_eq`. -/
theorem idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf_eq :
    Stacks.Sites.idealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
        (pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I) (⊤ : F.Submodule) =
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.sheafifySubmodule
        (Stacks.Sites.presheafSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
          (pullbackIdealPresheaf B S hS f hf I) (⊤ : F.Submodule).toSubmodule) := by
  rw [pullbackIdealSubsheaf_eq_sheafifySubmodule]
  exact Stacks.Sites.idealSmul_sheafifySubmodule_eq (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
    (M := F) (pullbackIdealPresheaf B S hS f hf I) (⊤ : F.Submodule)

/-- **A section of `f⁻¹I · F` is locally a combination of products of a restricted pulled-back
section of `I` with a section of `F`.**

This is the description of the multiple which the objectwise computation of a product over an
affine chart, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_presheafIdealSmul_of_mem_idealSmul_of_isAffine`,
consumes: the left factor there has to be read on sections, and the inverse-image ideal is only
given by generators. -/
theorem mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf_iff {W : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1}
    {x : F.val.obj (op W)} :
    x ∈ (Stacks.Sites.idealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
        (pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I) (⊤ : F.Submodule)).obj (op W) ↔
      ∃ T : Sieve W, T ∈ SmallEtale.topology B S hS Y.1 W ∧
        ∀ ⦃V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1⦄ (g : V ⟶ W), T g →
          F.val.map g.op x ∈ (Stacks.Sites.presheafSmul
            (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2) (pullbackIdealPresheaf B S hS f hf I)
            (⊤ : F.Submodule).toSubmodule).obj (op V) :=
  (idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf_eq B S hS f hf I F).symm.subst
    (motive := fun N ↦ x ∈ N.obj (op W) ↔ _)
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_sheafifySubmodule_iff

/-! ### The two objectwise products read as ideal multiples of sections -/


/-- The span of the products of an element of an ideal `A` with an element of a set `P` containing
every element is the multiple `A • ⊤`. -/
private theorem mem_span_smul_iff_mem_smul_top {R M : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [AddCommMonoid M]
    [Module R M] (A : Ideal R) (P : Set M) (hP : ∀ m, m ∈ P) (x : M) :
    x ∈ Submodule.span R {z : M | ∃ a : R, a ∈ A ∧ ∃ m ∈ P, z = a • m} ↔
      x ∈ A • (⊤ : Submodule R M) := by
  constructor
  · intro hx
    induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem z hz =>
      obtain ⟨a, ha, m, -, rfl⟩ := hz
      exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul ha Submodule.mem_top
    | zero => exact Submodule.zero_mem _
    | add _ _ _ _ h1 h2 => exact Submodule.add_mem _ h1 h2
    | smul r _ _ h1 => exact Submodule.smul_mem _ r h1
  · intro hx
    refine Submodule.smul_induction_on hx
      (fun r hr n _ => Submodule.subset_span ⟨r, hr, n, hP n, rfl⟩)
      fun u v hu hv => Submodule.add_mem _ hu hv

/-- **A section of `f_*F` over an étale chart `Q` of `X` lies in the objectwise product `I · f_*F`
exactly when it lies in the ideal multiple `I(Q) · (f_*F)(Q)`** of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pushforwardIdealMultipleSections`.

The objectwise product of `Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul` is the span of the products of a
section of `I` with a section of `f_*F`, and the ideal multiple of a submodule is the smallest
submodule containing those products; this identifies the two. -/
theorem mem_presheafIdealSmul_iff_mem_pushforwardIdealMultipleSections
    (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    {x : F.val.obj (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))} :
    x ∈ (Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2) I
        (⊤ : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).Submodule).toSubmodule).obj
        (op Q) ↔
      x ∈ pushforwardIdealMultipleSections B S hS f hf I F Q := by
  let _ := pushforwardChartModule B S hS f hf F Q
  have hP : ∀ n, n ∈ (⊤ : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).Submodule
      ).toSubmodule.obj (op Q) := fun n =>
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.toSubmodule_top
      (M := (smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F)).symm.subst
      (motive := fun N ↦ n ∈ N.obj (op Q)) trivial
  exact mem_span_smul_iff_mem_smul_top (R := chartSectionsRing B S hS X Q) _ _ hP x

/-- **A section of `f_*F` over an étale chart `Q` of `X` lies in the objectwise product `I · f_*F`
exactly when it lies in the multiple of `F(Q ×_X Y)` by the ideal generated by the pulled-back
sections of `I` over `Q`.**

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ideal_smul_pushforward_sections_eq_of_representable` read on the
objectwise product of the small étale site. -/
theorem mem_presheafIdealSmul_iff_mem_pullbackIdealMultipleSections
    (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    {x : F.val.obj (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))} :
    x ∈ (Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2) I
        (⊤ : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).Submodule).toSubmodule).obj
        (op Q) ↔
      x ∈ pullbackIdealMultipleSections B S hS f hf I F Q :=
  (mem_presheafIdealSmul_iff_mem_pushforwardIdealMultipleSections B S hS f hf I F Q).trans
    (Set.ext_iff.1 (ideal_smul_pushforward_sections_eq_of_representable B S hS f hf I F Q) x)

/-- The objectwise inverse-image ideal over an étale chart of `Y`, as an ideal of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSectionsRing`.

This is the same object as `(pullbackIdealPresheaf …).obj (op V)`, only with the ring of sections
spelled so that `Ideal.map` along `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSectionsRestrict` and the ideal
multiple of a module of sections elaborate; the note on
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSectionsIdeal` records the same obstruction. -/
abbrev pullbackChartIdeal (V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1) :
    Ideal (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y V) :=
  (pullbackIdealPresheaf B S hS f hf I).obj (op V)

/-- **A section of `F` lies in the objectwise product of the objectwise inverse-image ideal with
`F` exactly when it lies in the ideal multiple of the sections of `F`**, over every étale chart of
`Y`. -/
theorem mem_presheafSmul_pullbackIdealPresheaf_iff (V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1)
    {x : F.val.obj (op V)} :
    x ∈ (Stacks.Sites.presheafSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
        (pullbackIdealPresheaf B S hS f hf I) (⊤ : F.Submodule).toSubmodule).obj (op V) ↔
      x ∈ pullbackChartIdeal B S hS f hf I V •
        (⊤ : Submodule (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y V) (F.val.obj (op V))) := by
  have hP : ∀ n, n ∈ ((⊤ : F.Submodule).toSubmodule.obj (op V)) := fun n =>
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.toSubmodule_top (M := F)).symm.subst
      (motive := fun N ↦ n ∈ N.obj (op V)) trivial
  exact mem_span_smul_iff_mem_smul_top (R := chartSectionsRing B S hS Y V) _ _ hP x

/-- **Over the smaller of two affine charts, the multiple of the sections by a restricted ideal is
spanned by the restrictions of the multiple over the larger one.**

A section of the module over the smaller chart is a combination of restricted sections over the
larger one, because the module is cartesian on affine charts, and the product of a restricted
scalar with a restricted section is the restriction of the product.  This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_span_image_restrict_of_mem_presheafIdealSmul` for an arbitrary ideal
of the ring of the larger chart in place of the sections of a sheaf of ideals, which is the shape
the inverse-image ideal comes in. -/
theorem mem_span_image_restrict_of_mem_map_smul
    (hF : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts (hF := Y.2) F) {U V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1}
    (hU : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U))
    (hV : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V))
    (mm : V ⟶ U) (J : Ideal (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y U)) {y : F.val.obj (op V)}
    (hy : y ∈ Ideal.map (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y mm) J •
      (⊤ : Submodule (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y V) (F.val.obj (op V)))) :
    y ∈ Submodule.span (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y V)
      (chartSectionsRestrictFun B S hS Y F mm ''
        (↑(J • (⊤ : Submodule (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y U) (F.val.obj (op U)))) :
          Set (F.val.obj (op U)))) := by
  set P := Submodule.span (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y V)
    (chartSectionsRestrictFun B S hS Y F mm ''
      (↑(J • (⊤ : Submodule (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y U) (F.val.obj (op U)))) :
        Set (F.val.obj (op U))))
  have hQ : ∀ b ∈ J, ∀ w : F.val.obj (op V),
      chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y mm b • w ∈ P := by
    intro b hb w
    have hw := mem_span_range_restrict_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts B S hS Y F hF hU hV mm w
    induction hw using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem v hv =>
      obtain ⟨v₀, rfl⟩ := hv
      have h1 : chartSectionsRestrictFun B S hS Y F mm (b • v₀) ∈ P :=
        Submodule.subset_span ⟨b • v₀, Submodule.smul_mem_smul hb Submodule.mem_top, rfl⟩
      rwa [show chartSectionsRestrictFun B S hS Y F mm (b • v₀) =
        chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y mm b • chartSectionsRestrictFun B S hS Y F mm v₀ from
          F.val.map_smul mm.op b v₀] at h1
    | zero => rw [smul_zero]; exact P.zero_mem
    | add _ _ _ _ h1 h2 => rw [smul_add]; exact P.add_mem h1 h2
    | smul c v _ h1 =>
      rw [smul_smul, mul_comm, ← smul_smul]
      exact P.smul_mem c h1
  let Qi : Ideal (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y V) :=
    { carrier := {d | ∀ w : F.val.obj (op V), d • w ∈ P}
      add_mem' := fun h1 h2 w => by rw [add_smul]; exact P.add_mem (h1 w) (h2 w)
      zero_mem' := fun w => by rw [zero_smul]; exact P.zero_mem
      smul_mem' := fun c d hd w => by
        rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_smul]
        exact P.smul_mem c (hd w) }
  have hmapQ : Ideal.map (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y mm) J ≤ Qi :=
    Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.2 fun b hb => hQ b hb
  exact Submodule.smul_induction_on hy (fun r hr nn _ => hmapQ hr nn)
    fun u v hu hv => P.add_mem hu hv

/-! ### Descent of the opposite inclusion over an affine chart -/

/-- **The opposite inclusion of Stacks 0GF8 over an affine chart, granted that the objectwise
inverse-image ideal is already the pulled-back ideal over the affine charts above `Q ×_X Y`.**

For a chart `Q` of `X` whose base change `Q ×_X Y` is affine, and a module `F` cartesian on
affine charts, a section of `f⁻¹I · F` over `Q ×_X Y` lies in the objectwise product `I · f_*F`
over `Q`.

The section lies in the objectwise product of the objectwise inverse-image ideal with `F` along a
covering sieve of `Q ×_X Y`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf_iff`), which contains a finite
family of affine charts whose rings have a faithfully flat product over the ring of `Q ×_X Y`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.faithfullyFlat_pi_chartSectionsRing_of_ofArrows_mem_etalePrecoverage`).
Over each member the hypothesis turns that product into the multiple by the restricted pulled-back
ideal, which is spanned by the restrictions of the multiple over `Q ×_X Y` because `F` is
cartesian, so
`Submodule.mem_of_forall_mem_span_image_of_bijective_liftBaseChange` descends the membership; and
the multiple over `Q ×_X Y` is the objectwise product `I · f_*F` over `Q` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_presheafIdealSmul_iff_mem_pullbackIdealMultipleSections`. -/
theorem mem_presheafIdealSmul_of_mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf
    (hF : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts (hF := Y.2) F) (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (hbcQ : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
      ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q)))
    (hA : ∀ (V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1) (v : V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q),
      IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V) →
        pullbackChartIdeal B S hS f hf I V ≤
          Ideal.map (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y v)
            (Ideal.map (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q)
              (chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I Q)))
    {x : F.val.obj (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))}
    (hx : x ∈ (Stacks.Sites.idealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
      (pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I) (⊤ : F.Submodule)).obj
        (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))) :
    x ∈ (Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2) I
      (⊤ : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).Submodule).toSubmodule).obj
      (op Q) := by
  have hx' := (mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf_iff B S hS f hf I F).1 hx
  obtain ⟨T, hT, hmem⟩ := hx'
  have hcovbc := SmallEtale.exists_finite_affine_etale_ofArrows_le B S hS Y.1 hbcQ hT
  obtain ⟨_, z, φ, hzaff, hzT, -, hzet⟩ := hcovbc
  let algz : ∀ i, Algebra (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))
      (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y (z i)) := fun i ↦ chartSectionsRestrictAlgebra B S hS Y (φ i)
  let modz : ∀ i, Module (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))
      (F.val.obj (op (z i))) := fun i ↦ chartSectionsRestrictModule B S hS Y F (φ i)
  have towz : ∀ i, IsScalarTower
      (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))
      (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y (z i)) (F.val.obj (op (z i))) :=
    fun i ↦ chartSectionsRestrict_isScalarTower B S hS Y F (φ i)
  have hff := faithfullyFlat_pi_chartSectionsRing_of_ofArrows_mem_etalePrecoverage
    B S hS Y hbcQ z φ hzaff hzet
  have key : x ∈ Ideal.map (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q)
      (chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I Q) •
      (⊤ : Submodule (chartSectionsRing B S hS Y ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))
        (F.val.obj (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q)))) := by
    refine Submodule.mem_of_forall_mem_span_image_of_bijective_liftBaseChange
      (fun i ↦ chartSectionsRestrictLinear B S hS Y F (φ i))
      (fun i ↦ bijective_liftBaseChange_chartSectionsRestrictLinear B S hS Y F hF hbcQ
        (hzaff i) (φ i)) fun i ↦ ?_
    refine mem_span_image_restrict_of_mem_map_smul B S hS F hF hbcQ (hzaff i) (φ i) _ ?_
    refine Submodule.smul_le.2 (fun r hr nn hnn => Submodule.smul_mem_smul
      (hA (z i) (φ i) (hzaff i) hr) hnn) ?_
    exact (mem_presheafSmul_pullbackIdealPresheaf_iff B S hS f hf I F (z i)).1
      (hmem (φ i) (hzT i))
  exact (mem_presheafIdealSmul_iff_mem_pullbackIdealMultipleSections B S hS f hf I F Q).2 key

/-! ### Reduction to an affine chart of `X` -/

/-- **Membership in `I · f_*F` over an étale chart of `X` is a question about the affine charts
above it.**  A section of `f_*F` over a chart `Q` of `X` whose restriction to every affine chart
above `Q` lies in the objectwise product `I · f_*F` there lies in `I · f_*F` over `Q`.

The affine charts above `Q` cover it by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.exists_affine_etale_ofArrows`, and every arrow of the sieve
they generate factors through one of them, so the objectwise membership propagates to the whole
sieve and the local description of the product applies. -/
theorem mem_idealSmul_of_forall_isAffine (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    {x : F.val.obj (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))}
    (hx : ∀ (Q' : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (g : Q' ⟶ Q),
      IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj Q') →
      (((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).val.map g.op) x ∈
        (Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2) I
          (⊤ : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).Submodule).toSubmodule).obj
          (op Q')) :
    x ∈ (Stacks.Sites.idealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2) I
      (⊤ : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).Submodule)).obj (op Q) := by
  have hcovQ := SmallEtale.exists_affine_etale_ofArrows B S hS X.1 Q
  obtain ⟨_, Z, aa, hZaff, hcov, -⟩ := hcovQ
  refine Stacks.Sites.mem_idealSmul_of_mem (O := structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2)
    (M := (smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F) (I := I)
    (N := (⊤ : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).Submodule))
    (T := Sieve.ofArrows Z aa) hcov ?_
  rintro V v ⟨W, w, g, ⟨i⟩, rfl⟩
  have key : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).val.map (w ≫ aa i).op x =
      ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).val.map w.op
        (((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).val.map (aa i).op x) :=
    PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply
      ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).val (aa i).op w.op x
  exact (congrArg (· ∈ _) key).mpr <|
    (Stacks.Sites.presheafIdealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2) I
      (⊤ : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).Submodule).toSubmodule).map_mem
        w.op (hx (Z i) (aa i) (hZaff i))

/-! ### The opposite inclusion from the objectwise description of the inverse-image ideal -/

/-- **The opposite inclusion of Stacks 0GF8, granted that the objectwise inverse-image ideal is
already the pulled-back ideal over the affine charts above a base-changed affine chart.**

A section of `f_*F` over an étale chart `Q` of `X` lying in `f_*(f⁻¹I · F)` lies in `I · f_*F`.

Membership in `I · f_*F` over `Q` is a question about the affine charts above `Q`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_idealSmul_of_forall_isAffine`), over each of which it is the
descent statement
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_presheafIdealSmul_of_mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf`.

The two hypotheses are what the affine case of the tag still needs: that the base change of an
affine chart of `X` is an affine chart of `Y`, which holds for an affine `f`, and that over an
affine chart of `Y` above a base-changed affine chart the objectwise inverse-image ideal is
generated by the pulled-back sections from that one chart.  The latter is an identity between the
generators coming from two different charts `Q'` and `Q''` of `X`, and is proved by comparing both
over the product `Q' ×_X Q''`; see the implementation notes. -/
theorem mem_idealSmul_pushforward_of_mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf
    (hF : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts (hF := Y.2) F)
    (hbc : ∀ Q' : SmallEtale B S hS X.1,
      IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj Q') →
        IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
          ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q')))
    (hA : ∀ Q' : SmallEtale B S hS X.1,
      IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj Q') →
        ∀ (V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1) (v : V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q'),
        IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V) →
          pullbackChartIdeal B S hS f hf I V ≤
            Ideal.map (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y v)
              (Ideal.map (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q')
                (chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I Q')))
    (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    {x : F.val.obj (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))}
    (hx : x ∈ (Stacks.Sites.idealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
      (pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I) (⊤ : F.Submodule)).obj
        (op ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q))) :
    x ∈ (Stacks.Sites.idealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2) I
      (⊤ : ((smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS f hf).obj F).Submodule)).obj (op Q) := by
  refine mem_idealSmul_of_forall_isAffine B S hS f hf I F Q fun Q' g hQ' => ?_
  refine mem_presheafIdealSmul_of_mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I F hF Q'
    (hbc Q' hQ') (hA Q' hQ') ?_
  exact (Stacks.Sites.idealSmul (O := structureSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
    (pullbackIdealSubsheaf B S hS f hf I) (⊤ : F.Submodule)).toSubmodule.map_mem
      ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map g).op hx

end

